  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1256 PM CDT Wed Jul 1 2026\n\nThe remainder of this week into the Fourth of July favors dry and \nhot conditions under high pressure forecast to pinch off from its \nmore formidable cousin driving the excessive heat in the eastern \nCONUS. Fortunately, high temps off the Caprock are expected to \nfall shy of Heat Advisories with mostly mid/upper 90s elsewhere. \nBy Sunday afternoon and evening, ensembles agree in the high \nexiting west into New Mexico which would entertain low PoPs here \ncourtesy of ridge-riding shortwaves in NNW flow. This theme holds \nthrough the middle of next week with NW flow further amplifying \nfrom additional shortwaves in the central plains. Daily storm \nchances and seasonal temps look good at this time, although PoPs \nin later forecasts may need to be refined to favor the nighttime \nhours which is more typical of our NW flow regimes.",
